+# Northwind Traders
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Go-live | 2026-W44 (contract: `docs/NORTHWIND_SOW.md`) |
+| Account manager | not assigned in the registry yet |
+| Grain / timezone | 30 minutes / America/Chicago (DST) |
+| Operating hours | 06:00-24:00 local, seven days; vip contacts 08:00-20:00 |
+| Queues | priority 90/30, standard 80/20, vip 90/20 (Erlang C, occupancy <= 0.85) |
+| Working time | 40 h FT, 24 h PT, 11 h rest, 5 consecutive days |
+| Config | `configs/northwind.yaml` (schema 1) |
+| Roster | `data/agents/northwind.csv`, 51 agents (8 PT; 11 can take vip) |
+| Data | `data/northwind/export_<ISO>.csv`, local time with an authoritative `utc_offset` per row |
+
+## Run
+
+`python -m wfm run --client northwind --week <week>` writes `out/northwind/schedule.csv`, `eval.json`,
+`RUNBOOK.md` (SOW 3 table and handover note) and `exceptions.md` (SOW 2.7). A run takes about 40 s: the
+scheduler searches for the best vip attainment the roster allows.
+
+## Things to know
+
+- **DST.** The 2026-W44 export has 1,014 rows (169 elapsed hours): 2026-11-01 01:00-02:00 appears twice with
+  offsets -05:00 and -06:00. Ingest keeps both; never re-localise from the label.
+- **vip is roster-bound.** Eleven agents hold the vip skill (7 vip-only, 4 also priority). Covering every
+  vip interval needs more agent-hours than they can work under the 40 h cap and the rest rule, so vip
+  weekly attainment is below the 0.95 bound. For 2026-W44 the scheduler reaches 0.917 (154 of 168 intervals); a
+  relaxation that ignores rest, consecutive days and breaks still cannot do better than 13 short intervals
+  (0.923), so 0.95 is out of reach with this roster. The figure is in `exceptions.md`. This needs
+  raising with the account team (SOW 2.7): more vip-skilled agents, or cross-skilling priority agents.
+- **Breaks pile up.** SOW 2.3 puts every break in the interval with the largest gross surplus, so many
+  breaks land on the same interval. The scheduler plans against attainment net of breaks.
+- **Unusual rows.** The README asks for anything odd in the export to be reported to Northwind's WFM
+  contact. W42-W44 have no duplicate, negative or missing rows apart from the DST repeat above.
